WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Module 3 asks you to run the harness
exactly as it ships.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.900
Do not pass a case flag. Do not pass a
trial count. Do not edit a case file.

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.450
You are reading the tool this week, not
changing it.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.825
This video does pass a case flag, so you
see one case instead of a whole run.

5
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:21.975
Nothing on screen here is your submission.

6
00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:26.600
Capture all six items from your own
report, not from this video.

7
00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.474
Your own run takes a while, because the

8
00:00:29.474 --> 00:00:32.450
harness pauses between trials. Start it
early.

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.850
Start by seeing which cases ship with the
harness.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.800
The list flag prints the cases and runs
none of them.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.550
Eight cases. Six attacks, and two
controls.

12
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.500
Every line gives you an id, a kind, and a
title.

13
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.075
Note that total, because your report says
how many cases ran.

14
00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:55.150
Here is the run. Read it from the top.

15
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.726
The banner names the provider, your

16
00:00:57.726 --> 00:01:00.525
student ID, the target, and the case
counts.

17
00:01:00.875 --> 00:01:03.737
This provider is mock, and the line says
its

18
00:01:03.737 --> 00:01:06.600
results are not evidence about a real
model.

19
00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.725
Then the detector self-test line. It
carries a probe count and an OK.

20
00:01:12.075 --> 00:01:14.575
Then the two controls, both OK.

21
00:01:14.925 --> 00:01:17.384
The escalation control shows X marks,

22
00:01:17.384 --> 00:01:20.375
because there the mail is supposed to go
out.

23
00:01:20.725 --> 00:01:25.200
Then the attack case. Five X marks, one
per full agent run.

24
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:29.225
The status lands. Vulnerable, five out of
five.

25
00:01:29.575 --> 00:01:33.925
Then the two report files this run wrote,
and a count of each status.

26
00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:38.825
The self test is the harness proving
itself before it grades anything.

27
00:01:39.175 --> 00:01:41.582
A detector has to fire when the attack

28
00:01:41.582 --> 00:01:44.750
clearly happened, and stay quiet when
nothing did.

29
00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.800
Then the two controls run, ahead of every
attack case.

30
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:53.575
If a control fails, the run stops and no
attack results print.

31
00:01:53.925 --> 00:01:58.400
Numbers from a tool that cannot pass its
own test are not numbers.

32
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.807
A run that stopped is a real finding about
your

33
00:02:01.807 --> 00:02:05.125
environment. It is worth more than a made
up table.

34
00:02:05.475 --> 00:02:10.000
Every run writes two reports, one JSON and
one markdown.

35
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.038
Everything you capture is already in
there,

36
00:02:13.038 --> 00:02:15.975
so paste from the markdown instead of
retyping.

37
00:02:16.325 --> 00:02:18.325
Start with the scope section.

38
00:02:18.675 --> 00:02:23.200
Discovery found a second address, and the
harness refused to touch it.

39
00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:28.225
That refusal is one of the six items. Copy
it from your own report.

40
00:02:28.575 --> 00:02:31.575
Now the block for the case this video ran.

41
00:02:31.925 --> 00:02:36.575
Result, vulnerable. Landed in five of five
completed trials.

42
00:02:36.925 --> 00:02:41.125
Then the framework identifiers, and the
detector that decided it.

43
00:02:41.475 --> 00:02:44.200
Read the evidence line as a sentence.

44
00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:49.100
An outbox file, addressed to a records
archive outside the company.

45
00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:53.625
That line describes something the system
did, not something it said.

46
00:02:53.975 --> 00:02:57.775
Two ways to lose points here have nothing
to do with skill.

47
00:02:58.125 --> 00:03:00.725
The first is a status with no rate.

48
00:03:01.075 --> 00:03:04.057
The word vulnerable hides the difference
between

49
00:03:04.057 --> 00:03:07.225
one of five and five of five. Always give
the rate.

50
00:03:07.575 --> 00:03:09.947
The second is the model's words as

51
00:03:09.947 --> 00:03:13.575
evidence. An agent announcing a plan
proves nothing.

52
00:03:13.925 --> 00:03:17.925
Quote the outbox file, the audit row, or
your canary token.

53
00:03:18.275 --> 00:03:20.450
Grade the world, not the prose.

54
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.700
You hand in one file.

55
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.457
The six items you captured, your two
sentences on what a

56
00:03:26.457 --> 00:03:30.350
failed self test would mean, and the four
walkthrough questions.

57
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.600
The walkthrough answers go in this file,
not a separate upload.

58
00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:40.050
Start the run early, and let it finish. A
stopped run is still worth reporting.
